						<div id="render-table" class="main_wrapper_main mobile_grid" style="width: 100%; height: 100%;"><main class="main-wrapper" data-output-version="1" style="min-height: 100vh;"><div class="section_wrapper_117418" id="117418" x-data="{ customer: funnelish.session().customer }" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column;"><section data-eid="117418" class="section el-117418"><div class="section_row el-514517" data-eid="514517"><span id="514517" class="hidden-anchor"></span><div class="row-column" style="width: 100%;"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="580220"><div class="el-580220 img" is-popup="false"><div class="ksg-header-brand" style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;width:100%;height:55px;color:#ffffff;font-family:'Noto Serif',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.5px;">Modern Parenting Digest</div></div></div></div></div></section></div><div class="section_wrapper_652902" id="652902" x-data="{ customer: funnelish.session().customer }" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column;"><section data-eid="652902" class="section el-652902"><div class="section_row el-597579" data-eid="597579"><span id="597579" class="hidden-anchor"></span><div class="row-column" style="width: 100%;"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="797676"><div class="el-797676" is-popup="false"><div class="headline"><div class="headline-inner"><h2>5 Reasons a Kids' Encyclopedia Is the Best Way to Reduce Screen Time</h2></div></div></div></div><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="683539"><div class="el-683539" is-popup="false"><div class="paragraph"><div class="paragraph-inner"><p>One hardcover book left out on the coffee table. That is the whole trick. Most parents watch their kid reach for it on their own within a week, with no nagging and no nightly fight over the tablet.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="226123"><div class="el-226123 img" is-popup="false"><picture><source  media="(width &gt; 1024px)"><img style="object-fit:cover;object-position:center;" alt="" data-src="https://lp-096-prime-naturals.pages.dev/images/img-1.jpg" data- height="526px" src="https://lp-096-prime-naturals.pages.dev/images/img-1.jpg" width="100%" crossorigin="anonymous" fetchpriority="high"></picture></div></div><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="211172"><div class="el-211172" is-popup="false"><div class="paragraph"><div class="paragraph-inner"><p>Kids' books are not new. What makes the 10,000 Whys encyclopedia different is that children actually want to read it. It answers the real questions they ask all day, so it pulls them in the way a screen does, except it leaves them curious and calmer instead of wired.</p><p><br></p><p>The five reasons below cover what the book does, who it works for, and what most parents notice in the first week or two. The numbers come from a survey of real buyers. Pricing and the guarantee come straight from Prime Naturals.</p><p><br>Below: an honest look at the <span style="margin: 0px;"><strong>10,000 Whys Kids' Encyclopedia</strong></span>. Five reasons, one at a time.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="316990"><div class="el-316990" is-popup="false"><div class="headline"><div class="headline-inner"><h2><strong>What the 10,000 Whys Encyclopedia Actually Does</strong></h2></div></div></div></div><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="989718"><div class="container-wrapper container_989718"><div class="container el-989718"><div class="container-box cbox-989718-0"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="912048"><div class="container-wrapper container_912048"><div class="container el-912048" id="point-a"><div class="container-box cbox-912048-0"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="175701"><div class="el-175701" is-popup="false"><div class="headline"><div class="headline-inner"><p>1</p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="container-box cbox-912048-1"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="482194"><div class="el-482194" is-popup="false"><div class="headline"><div class="headline-inner"><h2>Kids Pick It Up On Their Own, No Nagging</h2></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="997424"><div class="el-997424 img" is-popup="false"><picture><source  media="(width &gt; 1024px)"><img alt="" data-src="https://lp-096-prime-naturals.pages.dev/images/img-2.png" data- height="auto" src="https://lp-096-prime-naturals.pages.dev/images/img-2.png" width="100%" crossorigin="anonymous" fetchpriority="high"></picture></div></div></div><div class="container-box cbox-989718-1"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="470141"><div class="container-wrapper container_470141"><div class="container el-470141" id="point-a"><div class="container-box cbox-470141-0"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="891843"><div class="el-891843" is-popup="false"><div class="headline"><div class="headline-inner"><p>1</p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="container-box cbox-470141-1"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="125848"><div class="el-125848" is-popup="false"><div class="headline"><div class="headline-inner"><h2>Kids Pick It Up On Their Own, No Nagging</h2></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="343381"><div class="container-wrapper container_343381"><div class="container el-343381"><div class="container-box cbox-343381-0"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="616114"><div class="el-616114" is-popup="false"><div class="paragraph"><div class="paragraph-inner"><p><span style="background-color: transparent; margin: 0px;">Here is the part that surprised me. Most books I bought my son just sat there. He is a screen kid, so I expected the same thing. I left this one on the coffee table and said nothing. By day three I found him on the floor at 9pm reading about black holes when I thought he was asleep. In a survey of 1,200 buyers, 97% of kids picked the book up without being asked after the first week.</span></p><p></p><p><span style="background-color: transparent; margin: 0px;">And there is nothing to set up. You leave the book where your kid will see it and let curiosity do the rest. No app to download, no timer to argue over. Honestly that is the only reason it has stuck around in our house.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="986984"><div class="container-wrapper container_986984"><div class="container el-986984"><div class="container-box cbox-986984-0"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="271092"><div class="el-271092" is-popup="false"><div class="paragraph"><div class="paragraph-inner"><p><span style="background-color: transparent; margin: 0px;"><strong>A real hardcover that kids love. Built for ages 6 to 12. Rated 4.9 stars across 2,847 reviews.</strong></span></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="374620"><div class="container-wrapper container_374620"><div class="container el-374620"><div class="container-box cbox-374620-0"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="310733"><div class="container-wrapper container_310733"><div class="container el-310733" id="point-a"><div class="container-box cbox-310733-0"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="509529"><div class="el-509529" is-popup="false"><div class="headline"><div class="headline-inner"><p>2</p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="container-box cbox-310733-1"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="653920"><div class="el-653920" is-popup="false"><div class="headline"><div class="headline-inner"><h2 style="text-align: left;">It Answers the Questions They'd Otherwise Google</h2></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="502734"><div class="el-502734 img" is-popup="false"><picture><source  media="(width &gt; 1024px)"><img alt="" data-src="https://lp-096-prime-naturals.pages.dev/images/img-3.png" data- height="auto" src="https://lp-096-prime-naturals.pages.dev/images/img-3.png" width="100%" crossorigin="anonymous" fetchpriority="high"></picture></div></div></div><div class="container-box cbox-374620-1"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="646410"><div class="container-wrapper container_646410"><div class="container el-646410" id="point-a"><div class="container-box cbox-646410-0"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="492237"><div class="el-492237" is-popup="false"><div class="headline"><div class="headline-inner"><p>2</p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="container-box cbox-646410-1"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="999199"><div class="el-999199" is-popup="false"><div class="headline"><div class="headline-inner"><h2 style="text-align: left;">It Answers the Questions They'd Otherwise Google</h2></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="93045"><div class="container-wrapper container_93045"><div class="container el-93045"><div class="container-box cbox-93045-0"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="416770"><div class="el-416770" is-popup="false"><div class="paragraph"><div class="paragraph-inner"><p><span style="background-color: transparent; margin: 0px;">If your kid fires off twenty questions a day and you end up handing over a phone to answer them, you know the pattern. One question turns into a video, then another video, then an hour is gone. This book answers the questions kids actually ask, from why kids have two eyes to how volcanoes work, so the screen never has to come out.</span></p><p></p><p><span style="background-color: transparent; margin: 0px;">The good part is you stop being the answer machine. Instead of saying ask me later or here, watch this, your kid goes and finds the answer themselves. One mom told us her 9-year-old read about vision, brains and evolution for 45 minutes, then came back and explained it to her.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="29615"><div class="container-wrapper container_29615"><div class="container el-29615"><div class="container-box cbox-29615-0"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="188529"><div class="el-188529" is-popup="false"><div class="paragraph"><div class="paragraph-inner"><p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin: 0px;">How it works: leave it somewhere they will spot it. One hardcover covers every subject a curious kid asks about. No app, no setup, no fuss. That is it.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="231462"><div class="container-wrapper container_231462"><div class="container el-231462"><div class="container-box cbox-231462-0"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="531769"><div class="container-wrapper container_531769"><div class="container el-531769" id="point-a"><div class="container-box cbox-531769-0"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="7660"><div class="el-7660" is-popup="false"><div class="headline"><div class="headline-inner"><p>3</p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="container-box cbox-531769-1"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="935432"><div class="el-935432" is-popup="false"><div class="headline"><div class="headline-inner"><h2 style="text-align: left;">Every Subject They're Curious About, In One Book</h2></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="696085"><div class="el-696085 img" is-popup="false"><picture><source  media="(width &gt; 1024px)"><img alt="" data-src="https://lp-096-prime-naturals.pages.dev/images/img-4.png" data- height="auto" src="https://lp-096-prime-naturals.pages.dev/images/img-4.png" width="100%" crossorigin="anonymous" fetchpriority="high"></picture></div></div></div><div class="container-box cbox-231462-1"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="965236"><div class="container-wrapper container_965236"><div class="container el-965236" id="point-a"><div class="container-box cbox-965236-0"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="77093"><div class="el-77093" is-popup="false"><div class="headline"><div class="headline-inner"><p>3</p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="container-box cbox-965236-1"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="702628"><div class="el-702628" is-popup="false"><div class="headline"><div class="headline-inner"><h2 style="text-align: left;">Every Subject They're Curious About, In One Book</h2></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="544659"><div class="container-wrapper container_544659"><div class="container el-544659"><div class="container-box cbox-544659-0"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="835356"><div class="el-835356" is-popup="false"><div class="paragraph"><div class="paragraph-inner"><p><span style="background-color: transparent; margin: 0px;">Here's the thing nobody tells you: kids don't reach for screens because they love screens. They reach for them because that is where the interesting stuff lives. Animals, space, the human body, nature, technology, daily life. When all of it sits in one book they can flip through, the screen stops being the only door to it.</span></p><p></p><p><span style="background-color: transparent; margin: 0px;">Because every topic lives in one place, there is no rabbit hole and no autoplay. A question about sharks does not turn into an hour of recommended videos. They find the answer, then move on to the next thing they wondered about, the way reading is supposed to work.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="445047"><div class="container-wrapper container_445047"><div class="container el-445047"><div class="container-box cbox-445047-0"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="635755"><div class="el-635755" is-popup="false"><div class="paragraph"><div class="paragraph-inner"><p><span style="background-color: transparent; margin: 0px;">One hardcover covering animals, space, the body, nature, technology and daily life.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="691127"><div class="container-wrapper container_691127"><div class="container el-691127"><div class="container-box cbox-691127-0"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="887229"><div class="container-wrapper container_887229"><div class="container el-887229" id="point-a"><div class="container-box cbox-887229-0"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="350079"><div class="el-350079" is-popup="false"><div class="headline"><div class="headline-inner"><p>4</p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="container-box cbox-887229-1"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="482889"><div class="el-482889" is-popup="false"><div class="headline"><div class="headline-inner"><h2>It Builds Real Thinking, Not Just Scrolling</h2></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="492076"><div class="el-492076 img" is-popup="false"><picture><source  media="(width &gt; 1024px)"><img alt="" data-src="https://lp-096-prime-naturals.pages.dev/images/img-5.jpg" data- height="auto" src="https://lp-096-prime-naturals.pages.dev/images/img-5.jpg" width="100%" crossorigin="anonymous" fetchpriority="high"></picture></div></div></div><div class="container-box cbox-691127-1"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="82482"><div class="container-wrapper container_82482"><div class="container el-82482" id="point-a"><div class="container-box cbox-82482-0"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="134535"><div class="el-134535" is-popup="false"><div class="headline"><div class="headline-inner"><p>4</p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="container-box cbox-82482-1"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="643928"><div class="el-643928" is-popup="false"><div class="headline"><div class="headline-inner"><h2>It Builds Real Thinking, Not Just Scrolling</h2></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="518195"><div class="container-wrapper container_518195"><div class="container el-518195"><div class="container-box cbox-518195-0"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="335957"><div class="el-335957" is-popup="false"><div class="paragraph"><div class="paragraph-inner"><p><span style="background-color: transparent; margin: 0px;">A kid can stare at a screen for hours and come away with nothing. Watching is not the same as thinking. Reading makes them stop, picture it, and connect one idea to the next. Parents notice the difference fast. In the same survey, 94% said their child's school performance improved within 60 days, and 91% said their kid started asking deeper questions.</span></p><p></p><p><span style="background-color: transparent; margin: 0px;">Jennifer told us her daughter had never picked up a book without being forced. She left this one out on a Friday. By Sunday her daughter had read half of it and was explaining to her grandfather, a retired engineer, why the moon doesn't fall out of the sky. He was impressed.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="223634"><div class="container-wrapper container_223634"><div class="container el-223634"><div class="container-box cbox-223634-0"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="17989"><div class="el-17989" is-popup="false"><div class="paragraph"><div class="paragraph-inner"><p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin: 0px;">94% of parents saw school performance improve within 60 days, from a survey of 1,200 buyers.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="353348"><div class="container-wrapper container_353348"><div class="container el-353348"><div class="container-box cbox-353348-0"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="131679"><div class="container-wrapper container_131679"><div class="container el-131679" id="point-a"><div class="container-box cbox-131679-0"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="253331"><div class="el-253331" is-popup="false"><div class="headline"><div class="headline-inner"><p>5</p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="container-box cbox-131679-1"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="952359"><div class="el-952359" is-popup="false"><div class="headline"><div class="headline-inner"><h2>It Turns Screen Time Into a Reading Habit</h2></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="995567"><div class="el-995567 img" is-popup="false"><picture><source  media="(width &gt; 1024px)"><img alt="" data-src="https://lp-096-prime-naturals.pages.dev/images/img-6.png" data- height="auto" src="https://lp-096-prime-naturals.pages.dev/images/img-6.png" width="100%" crossorigin="anonymous" fetchpriority="high"></picture></div></div></div><div class="container-box cbox-353348-1"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="254098"><div class="container-wrapper container_254098"><div class="container el-254098" id="point-a"><div class="container-box cbox-254098-0"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="560824"><div class="el-560824" is-popup="false"><div class="headline"><div class="headline-inner"><p>5</p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="container-box cbox-254098-1"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="968675"><div class="el-968675" is-popup="false"><div class="headline"><div class="headline-inner"><h2>It Turns Screen Time Into a Reading Habit</h2></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="575486"><div class="container-wrapper container_575486"><div class="container el-575486"><div class="container-box cbox-575486-0"><div class="element-wrapper" data-eid="739692"><div class="el-739692" is-popup="false"><div class="paragraph"><div class="paragraph-inner"><p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin: 0px;">Here's the part that actually changed things for us. A screen gives a kid a quick hit and leav